/* wang19_fig3_neg_demonic_lb.qhes with the round counter read as an integer, as
   the program of Wang, Fu, Goharshady, Chatterjee, Qin and Shi, PLDI 2019,
   Fig. 3 has it (x0 = 100, one round per decrement).  The value is 2.475 * x
   at every integer x >= 0, exactly 247.5 at x = 100; over a real x it is
   2.475 * floor(x), which no linear lower bound valid at every real state
   reaches at x = 100. */
X 100 >= 247.5
s.t.
X (x : int) : real =mu
  if x >= 1 then
    0.0005 * (0.99 * (X (x - 1) + 5000.0) + 0.01 * min (X (x - 1) + 5000.0) (X (x - 1))) +
    0.9995 * X (x - 1)
  else 0.0;
